			<div class="content" id="post-content-2089492">
									

<p>Thank you for giving critique on the article, Esko.</p>
<p>EchoFourDelta pointed out something like this earlier, saying the entire article didn't make sense (resulting in me going back to edit it some more). I'm sorry if some of the details didn't come across as clear to you.</p>
<p>The very first line in the containment procedures is one I've used verbatim on another SCP. That line was also one I took from an older SCP. Both cases of it being used has worked well to my knowledge.</p>
<p>In short, the name (if you were to research it in-universe), results in you learning about a Caucasian man (which is common, but not always true). Learning the name makes you think you are the man. The disputes makes them &quot;overwrite&quot; the original information they've received when they <em>first</em> became instances, essentially creating a new identity for them.</p>
<p>&quot;Safe information&quot; refers to information that has been confirmed to not cause SCP-2150 infection. The O5 are able to receive said info without coming into contact with the anomaly. Whatever &quot;info&quot; they receive is done so indirectly. The &quot;Original Documentation&quot; is the first written document of 2150.</p>
<p>Also, I was careful of making sure there was no direct implication of the O5 being infected. The last letter states that they have no knowledge of the name (except for the retired O5 member).</p>
<p>Everything else you have pointed out has been fixed accordingly. Thank you once again. Your input helps me to become a better writer.</p>
<p>If anything else comes off an unclear, feel free to ask.</p>

